# Lab names the lab's own resolver does not serve, answered by this box's
# dnsmasq instead. Same layout as /etc/hosts: an address, then one or more
# names. server-bootstrap.sh turns each line into a host-record in
# /etc/dnsmasq.d/lab-split-dns.conf, so a change here takes effect on the next
# run of that script.
#
# Every name must sit inside set.lab. Only that zone is pointed at this box
# (/etc/resolver/set.lab on the clients), so a record for any other name is
# never asked for. The address must also be reachable from the clients, which
# in practice means inside 10.47.0.0/16: a name that resolves to an address
# with no route still fails, only later.

10.47.7.47   git.gpu.set.lab
